  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Renewable energy from wind is the process of converting the natural, continuously
    replenished movement of air in Earth\u2019s atmosphere into usable electrical
    power. A windmill\u2014more accurately called a wind turbine in modern energy
    systems\u2014captures this moving air with large blades that rotate when the
    wind blows.\n\nAs the blades turn, they spin a central shaft connected to a generator,
    which produces electricity without burning fuel, releasing emissions, or consuming
    finite resources. Because wind is created by the Sun\u2019s uneven heating of
    Earth\u2019s surface, it is inexhaustible, clean, and sustainable.\n\nWind\u2011powered
    systems are used worldwide to reduce reliance on fossil fuels, lower greenhouse\u2011gas
    emissions, and support a transition to long\u2011term, environmentally responsible
    energy production."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
