  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "A fossil\u2011fuel power plant is a facility that generates electricity
    by burning coal, oil, or natural gas\u2014fuels formed from ancient plant and
    animal matter over millions of years.\n\nInside the plant, the fuel is burned
    in a large boiler to heat water into high\u2011pressure steam. This steam spins
    a turbine, which turns a generator to produce electricity.\n\nWhile fossil\u2011fuel
    plants have powered cities and industries for more than a century, they rely
    on finite resources and produce significant emissions, including carbon dioxide
    and air pollutants. Because these fuels take millions of years to form and are
    consumed far faster than they are created, they are non\u2011renewable."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
