  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Solar energy is the conversion of sunlight, a naturally renewed and virtually
    limitless resource, into usable electrical power. A solar panel, also called
    a photovoltaic (PV) panel, is made of special semiconductor materials that absorb
    light from the Sun.\n\nWhen sunlight strikes these materials, it frees tiny charged
    particles called electrons, creating an electric current. This process\u2014known
    as the photovoltaic effect\u2014allows solar panels to generate electricity without
    burning fuel, producing emissions, or consuming finite resources.\n\nBecause
    the Sun continuously delivers far more energy to Earth than humanity uses, solar
    power is considered clean, sustainable, and widely accessible. Solar panels are
    used on homes, buildings, and large solar farms to provide reliable electricity
    while reducing environmental impact.\n\nSee how they work here with the press
    of a button."
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
